# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform does. Git on Windows
# converts to CRLF by default, and a `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` shebang fails on Linux with
# the famously unhelpful "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — the deploy script
# is authored on Windows and runs in CI, so it would hit exactly that.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the mirror case: keep it CRLF so Windows tooling reads it natively.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
